<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch state lowers price of Feb 2007 bond to 99.50.</title>
<headline>Dutch state lowers price of Feb 2007 bond to 99.50.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Dutch Finance Ministry's capital markets agency lowered the price of the 5.75 percent bond due February 2007 to 99.50 from 99.75 on the second day of tap sales on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The capital markets agency said on Tuesday that 1.9 billion guilders had been raised so far through tap sales.</p>
<p>Tap sales of the bond, first issued in January, reopened on Tuesday and sales will continue from 0700 GMT to 1500 GMT each day until further notice.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
